# Creating a new API service

Read `architecture.mdc` and `running-tests.mdc` before changing code. One **API service** is one HTTP operation. Add it to an existing controller when the aggregate already has one. Create a controller only for a new aggregate.

Health, readiness, OpenAPI, and the local admin token route are closures. They are not domain use cases.

## Example

`GET /api/public/scammers/suggest?q=Acme` returns up to five scammer names. The pieces below are that operation. Copy the shape, not the query.

Request path: route → controller → command → use case → repository. The controller never calls a repository, Eloquent, or a concrete use case.

## 1. Route

Public routes live in `routes/api.public.php` under the `public` prefix and `throttle:public-api`. Laravel mounts that file at `/api`, so the URL is `/api/public/...`.

```php
Route::get('scammers/suggest', [ScammerController::class, 'suggest']);
```

Declare static paths (`scammers/suggest`) before `scammers/{id}`.

Admin routes live in `routes/api.admin.php`. Keep the existing group middleware: `auth:sanctum`, `EnsureUserIsActive`, `abilities:admin:write`, `can:manage-fraud-data`, `throttle:admin`, `AuditApiRequest`. Auth routes live in `routes/api.auth.php`.

## 2. Controller

`app/Http/Controllers/Public/ScammerController.php` type-hints the use-case interface and builds the command.

```php
public function __construct(private ScammerUsecaseInterface $scammers) {}

public function suggest(Request $request)
{
    $query = $request->input('q');

    return response()->json($this->scammers->suggest(new SuggestScammersCommand(is_string($query) ? $query : '')));
}
```

Keep status codes and JSON here:

- Invalid path id, page, or count: `400` with `{"message": "..."}`. Check ids with `filter_var($id, FILTER_VALIDATE_INT)`.
- Missing record: `404` with `{"message": "..."}`.
- A model: `(new ScammerResource($scammer))->resolve()`.
- A page: `{"data": ContactResource::collection($result->items)->resolve(), "total", "page", "count"}`. `p` is page (1–100000, default 1). `c` is page size (1–100, default 10).
- A created record: `201`.

A JSON body uses a `FormRequest` in `app/Http/Requests/{Public|Admin}/`. `StoreScammerContactRequest` is the pattern: `authorize()` returns `true` on public routes, and `rules()` describes the body. The controller passes `$request->validated()` into `CreateScammerContactCommand::fromValidated(...)`. Invalid bodies become `422` through the handler in `bootstrap/app.php` (`error.code = validation_failed`). Do not validate the body again in the use case.

## 3. Command

One readonly command per use-case method, in `app/Application/{Domain}/Commands/`.

```php
namespace App\Application\Scammer\Commands;

final readonly class SuggestScammersCommand
{
    public function __construct(
        public string $query,
    ) {}
}
```

Constructors take already-parsed values. A `fromValidated` factory belongs on the command when the controller has a validated array, as on `CreateScammerContactCommand`. Commands may use `App\Domain`, other commands, `App\Models`, and vendor classes. They must not use repositories, HTTP, or infrastructure.

## 4. Use case

Add the method to the interface and the class under `app/Application/{Domain}/Usecases/`. The method accepts that one command and returns the model, `PaginatedResult`, `MapResult`, array, or null the controller needs.

```php
public function suggest(SuggestScammersCommand $command): array
{
    return $this->scammers->suggest($command->query);
}
```

Type-hint repository interfaces in the constructor. Wrap multi-write work in `DB::transaction`, as `createContact` does. Map domain exceptions to HTTP only in the controller.

A new aggregate also needs `{Name}UsecaseInterface`, `{Name}Usecase`, and this binding in `app/Providers/AppServiceProvider.php`:

```php
$this->app->bind(SeoUsecaseInterface::class, SeoUsecase::class);
```

## 5. Repository

Add the read or write to the aggregate repository interface and its Eloquent implementation in `app/Repositories/{Domain}/`. Search cards stay on `*CardRepository`, not on the aggregate repository.

```php
public function suggest(string $query): array
{
    $query = trim($query);

    if (mb_strlen($query) < 2 || mb_strlen($query) > 100) {
        return [];
    }

    return Cache::remember(/* key, ttl, query */);
}
```

Pivot attaches go through that repository. `SearchCache` invalidation for attach-only writes stays inside the repository. A new repository interface gets a `bind` next to the others in `AppServiceProvider`.

External systems get a port interface in `Application` and an implementation in `Infrastructure`. Image storage goes through `TemporaryImageStorageInterface`.

## 6. OpenAPI

Add the path to `openapi.yaml`. Paths are relative to the `/api` server. Reuse `#/components/parameters/ScammerId` and `#/components/responses/RateLimited`. Put reusable bodies in `schemas/` and reference them with `$ref: ./schemas/Scammer.yaml`. `OpenApiDocument` bundles those files; there is no separate registration step.

`/public/scammers/suggest` uses `operationId: suggestScammerNames`, documents the `q` query param, and returns a string array capped at 5. Update the `info.description` when the new operation changes a public rule.

## 7. Tests

Add a feature test beside the controller's existing test, `tests/Feature/PublicScammerControllerTest.php`. Hit the real URL. Cover the success body, validation, not-found, and empty or boundary input. `test_suggest_scammer_names_by_partial_case_insensitive_query` is the success case: it creates scammers with factories and asserts the exact JSON.

Run inside the worktree's PHP container, in this order: `php artisan test`, `composer analyse`, `composer check:architecture`. See `running-tests.mdc`.

## New aggregate checklist

- `app/Domain/{Aggregate}/` for entities, enums, and value objects this operation needs.
- Model, factory, and migration when the table is new.
- Repository interface, Eloquent implementation, and provider binding.
- Use case interface, use case, command, and provider binding.
- Controller, route, resource or `FormRequest`, OpenAPI path, and feature test.

## Do not

- Call a repository or a concrete use case from a controller.
- Pass a raw request array into a use case.
- Put HTTP status codes or `FormRequest` classes in `Application`.
- Depend on `App\Http` or `App\Infrastructure` from a use case, or on anything outside `App\Domain` and vendor from the domain.
- Add a use case for health, readiness, OpenAPI, or the local admin token route.
